        "body": "### What should we add?\n\nCurrently, the addon only provides low-level functions, leaving it to the user to implement the configuration recovery loop manually (for example, see the second to last code cell of https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-sqd/tutorials/01_chemistry_hamiltonian.html). We should provide a high-level function to run the entire SQD algorithm, so that the user doesn't need to do so much manual work. It will also make it easier to implement improvements to the algorithm such as https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-addon-sqd/issues/192. Here is my proposal for the function signature:\n```python\ndef run_sqd(\n    h1e: np.ndarray,\n    h2e: np.ndarray,\n    nelec: tuple[int, int],\n    counts: dict[str, int],\n    subsample_size: int,\n    *,\n    initial_state: SCIState | None = None,\n    iterations: int = 1,\n    open_shell: bool = False,\n    spin_sq: float = 0.0,\n    n_subsamples: int = 1,\n    max_davidson_cycles: int = 200,\n    nuclear_repulsion_energy: float = 0.0,\n    callback,\n    seed: int | np.random.Generator | None = None,\n) -> tuple[float, SCIState]:\n```",
        "reactions": {
